Here’s the **clean and correct** pointer update for **Doubly Linked List – Delete at Beginning** 👇

---

### 🔹 Case 1 — List has **more than one** node

Steps:

```
ptr = head;
head = head->next;
head->prev = NULL;
free(ptr);
```

✔ New head’s `prev` must be set to `NULL`  
✔ No links lost

---

### 🔹 Case 2 — List has **only one** node

```
ptr = head;
head = NULL;
free(ptr);
```

✔ List becomes empty

---

### ⚠ Don’t forget to check empty list

```
if (head == NULL)
{
    printf("List empty");
}
```

---

### Full short function (exam-friendly)

```c
void deleteBegin()
{
    struct Node *ptr;
    if (head == NULL)
    {
        printf("List Empty");
        return;
    }

    ptr = head;
    if (head->next == NULL) // only one node
    {
        head = NULL;
    }
    else
    {
        head = head->next;
        head->prev = NULL;
    }

    free(ptr);
}
```

